<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46508" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sulcātor</span></b> , ōris,
			m.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>one who draws furrows</i>, <i>a furrower</i>,
				<i>plougher</i> (in postAug. poets).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Leontini campi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prud. adv. Symm. 2, 939</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">patuli agri,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Avien. Perieg. 587</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>one who sails
			over</i>, <i>traverses</i>, etc.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sulcator navita ponti,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					7, 363</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pigri Averni,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Charon</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 11, 588</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">undae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 8, 18</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bagrada sulcator harenae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					4, 588</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A render</i>, <i>tearer</i>, <i>lacerator</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lateris sulcator (vultur),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Claud. Rapt. Pros. 2, 340</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
